  "result": "I fixed the clamping bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. I haven't run the tests or added a new one.\n\nFor an open bound, the clamp moved the value the wrong way (`bound - dir`), so the result landed outside the allowed range. For example, `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True)` returned `-1` for an input of `-5`, when the nearest valid value is `1`. Similarly, `max_open=True` with a max of 10 returned `11` instead of `9`. It now uses `bound + dir`, which steps back inside the range.\n\nClosed ranges were never affected, since they return the bound itself. `FloatRange` rejects clamping on open bounds, so it was unaffected too.",
